     [ -f CLAUDE.md ] || cat > CLAUDE.md <<'MD'
 # Roblox Studio on a phone
 
-Roblox Studio is open beside you and connected through the Roblox_Studio MCP tools:
-`run_code` (run Luau in Studio and get what it prints), `insert_model`, `get_console_output`,
-`start_stop_play`, `run_script_in_play_mode` and `get_studio_mode`.
+Roblox Studio is open beside you and connected through the Roblox_Studio MCP tools.
 
-- Build by running Luau with `run_code`: create Parts, Models, Scripts (set `.Source`), etc. in the
-  open place. Check what is there first (e.g. list `workspace:GetChildren()`).
-- Studio runs on a phone through emulation and draws 3D on the processor: it is slow. Batch work
-  into a few larger `run_code` calls, keep scenes light (few parts, no huge terrain), and expect
-  each call to take seconds.
+Every call is a round trip of seconds, because Studio runs here under x86 emulation. So use the tool
+that takes the whole job at once instead of several `run_code` calls:
+
+| tool | use it for |
+|---|---|
+| `get_tree` | the instance tree in one call. Never walk `GetChildren()` with `run_code`. |
+| `get_properties` | several properties of one instance at once |
+| `set_properties` | several properties set at once, with `{"Vector3":[x,y,z]}`, `{"Color3":[r,g,b]}`, `{"UDim2":[xs,xo,ys,yo]}`, `{"Enum":"Material.Plastic"}` values |
+| `write_script` | create or replace a Script/LocalScript/ModuleScript and set its code |
+| `run_batch` | several Luau snippets in ONE round trip, each with its own result or error |
+| `run_code` | anything the above do not cover |
+| `insert_model` | a model from the marketplace |
+| `start_stop_play`, `run_script_in_play_mode`, `get_studio_mode`, `get_console_output` | testing |
+
+Paths are lists of child names from `game`, e.g. `["Workspace","Model","Part"]`, so a name with a
+dot, a space or a quote in it works.
+
+- Put a script's code in `write_script`, not in a `.Source` assignment inside `run_code`. The quoting
+  into Luau is done for you and handles quotes, backslashes, `]]` and control characters.
+- Look before you build: one `get_tree` tells you what is already there.
+- Keep scenes light (few parts, no huge terrain) and expect each call to take seconds.
 - Use `start_stop_play` to test, `get_console_output` to read errors, then stop play mode again.
+- If building feels slow, set the Build performance preset (Roblox Studio app -> Performance preset
+  -> Build): the 3D view drops to 40k pixels, which leaves the processor to your Luau instead of to
+  drawing a view nobody is looking at while you work. Put it back to Potato to look at the result.
 - If a tool says Studio is not connected: Studio is still starting, no place is open, or the MCP
   plugin needs permission to reach localhost (Studio asks once).
 MD
